{"step_index":443,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T10:37:20Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Create the backend for the NEXUS project.\r\n\r\nTechnology:\r\n\r\n* Python 3.12+\r\n* FastAPI\r\n* Pydantic\r\n* SQLAlchemy\r\n* CORS\r\n* Uvicorn\r\n\r\nCreate this structure:\r\n\r\nbackend/\r\napp/\r\nmain.py\r\napi/\r\nmodels/\r\nschemas/\r\nservices/\r\nutils/\r\nrequirements.txt\r\n\r\nCreate initial API endpoints:\r\n\r\nGET /health\r\nGET /api/cases\r\nGET /api/cases/{case_id}\r\nPOST /api/cases\r\nPOST /api/upload\r\nGET /api/network/{case_id}\r\nGET /api/entities/{entity_id}\r\nGET /api/insights/{case_id}\r\n\r\nUse mock data initially.\r\n\r\nEnable CORS for the React frontend.\r\n\r\nAdd clear error handling and API documentation through FastAPI's automatic docs.\r\n\r\nDo not implement authentication yet.\r\n\n2. I reviewed the backend implementation plan. Please revise it before writing the code.\r\n\r\nKeep the existing React/Vite frontend unchanged and create the backend alongside it.\r\n\r\nImportant changes:\r\n\r\n1. This is a simple working prototype, not a production system.\r\n2. Use only fictional synthetic Indian data.\r\n3. Use the case name \"Operation Chakravyuh\".\r\n4. Use Indian names such as Rahul Verma, Amit Yadav, Priya Singh, Suresh Sharma, and Neha Gupta.\r\n5. Use Indian locations such as Delhi, Ghaziabad, Noida, Lucknow, and Mirzapur.\r\n6. Use masked Indian phone numbers, fictional vehicle numbers such as UP14 AB 1234, and INR transaction values.\r\n7. Clearly label the dataset as \"Synthetic Investigation Dataset\".\r\n8. Start with 6–8 entities, 8–12 relationships, 1–2 possible patterns, and 2–3 evidence files.\r\n9. Use SQLite for the prototype.\r\n10. Explicitly include NetworkX for graph construction and basic analysis.\r\n11. Do not add Neo4j, PostgreSQL, authentication, OCR, PDF/DOCX processing, or advanced AI \n<truncated 912 bytes>\n3. The backend has been implemented, but I cannot open the local API.\nThe generated links are:\nSwagger UI: [http://localhost:8000/docssvg](http://localhost:8000/docssvg)\nHealth Check: [http://localhost:8000/health](http://localhost:8000/health)\nPlease diagnose the issue step by step.\nCheck the actual backend project location.\nCheck whether app.main:app imports successfully.\nCheck whether port 8000 is running.\nCheck the FastAPI application configuration.\nConfirm the correct Swagger URL. It should normally be /docs, not /docssvg.\nCheck whether the backend has startup errors.\nCheck whether CORS is configured for http://localhost:5173.\nRun the backend using:\npython -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\nTest these endpoints:\nGET /health\nGET /docs\nGET /openapi.json\nGET /api/cases\nDo not change the frontend yet.\nIf there is an error, show me the exact terminal error and explain what caused it before making changes.\n4. The backend is now running on:\n[http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000/)\nThe frontend is running on:\n[http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173/)\nPlease inspect the existing frontend and connect it to the backend APIs.\nRequirements:\nDo not redesign the frontend.\nDo not remove existing UI components.\nReplace only the relevant mock-data calls with API calls.\nCreate a central API configuration file.\nUse this backend base URL:\n[http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000/)\nConnect these endpoints first:\nGET /api/cases\nGET /api/cases/{case_id}\nGET /api/network/{case_id}\nGET /api/entities/{entity_id}\nGET /api/insights/{case_id}\nKeep a loading state and an error state.\nIf the backend is unavailable, show a clear error message.\nDo not add Gemini API integration yet.\nDo not change the backend structure.\nFirst inspect the frontend files and explain which files need to be changed. Then implement the connection and test it.\n5. host \n6. host\n7. @[Quote] \n8. host bro \n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Objective**: Create the backend for the NEXUS intelligence analytics platform, connect the existing React/Vite frontend to it without altering UI components or layout, and host/run both services concurrently.\n- **Backend Stack & Endpoints**: Python 3.12+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLite (`nexus.db`), NetworkX (topological metrics), Uvicorn.\n  - Endpoints: `GET /health`, `GET /api/cases`, `GET /api/cases/{case_id}`, `POST /api/cases`, `POST /api/upload` (restricted to TXT/CSV/JSON with `extraction_service.py`), `GET /api/network/{case_id}`, `GET /api/entities/{entity_id}`, `GET /api/insights/{case_id}`.\n- **Constraints & Ethics**:\n  - Strictly synthetic Indian investigation dataset (\"Operation Chakravyuh\").\n  - Fictional names (Rahul Verma, Amit Yadav, Priya Singh, Suresh Sharma, Neha Gupta), locations (Delhi, Ghaziabad, Noida, Lucknow, Mirzapur), vehicle `UP14 AB 1234`, masked phones, INR amounts.\n  - Ethical AI terminology: never label individuals as \"criminals\"; use `subject_of_interest`, `requires human review`, `possible pattern`, `risk indicator`.\n- **Frontend Scope**: Keep UI intact; replace relevant mock-data calls with live API calls (`http://localhost:8000`); maintain loading and graceful fallback/error states via `ApiStatusBanner`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Backend (`scratch/backend/`)**: 100% complete and tested.\n  - Models (`case.py`, `entity.py`, `evidence.py`, `base.py`), schemas, and services (`mock_data.py`, `case_service.py`, `entity_service.py`, `network_service.py` with NetworkX, `insight_service.py`, `extraction_service.py`, `upload_service.py`).\n  - Automated tests (`tests/test_phase1.py` and `tests/test_upload.py`) verified 100% passing.\n- **Frontend Accidental Deletion & Recovery**:\n  - `scratch/nexus` was accidentally removed by a user PowerShell command (`Remove-Item .\\NEXUS -Recurse -Force`, which on Windows NTFS deleted `.\\nexus`).\n  - Restored all 45 source files using `scratch/restore_nexus.py` by pulling full code blocks from previous conversation transcripts (`fb69bf55` and `296415ce`).\n  - Executed `npm install` in `scratch/nexus` (completed with 109 packages, 0 vulnerabilities).\n  - Fixed `src/main.tsx` (restored standard Vite React 19 root mounting).\n  - Updated `tsconfig.app.json` compiler options (`noUnusedLocals: false`, `noUnusedParameters: false`, `verbatimModuleSyntax: false`, `strict: false`).\n- **Incomplete / In-Progress**:\n  - `npm run build` in `scratch/nexus` flagged missing types (`TimelineEvent`, `EventCategory`) in `src/types/index.ts`, missing export `mockTimelineEvents` in `src/data/mockData.ts`, and an invalid import path `../../lib/utils` in `src/pages/TimelinePage.tsx`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Windows File System Trap**: Windows NTFS is case-insensitive, so commands targeting `.\\NEXUS` will delete or mutate `.\\nexus`.\n- **TypeScript Discrepancies**:\n  - `src/types/index.ts` requires `TimelineEvent` and `EventCategory` exports:\n    ```typescript\n    export type EventCategory = 'wiretap' | 'financial' | 'sighting' | 'border' | 'warrant' | 'comm';\n    export interface TimelineEvent {\n      id: string; timestamp: string; title: string; description: string;\n      category: EventCategory; entityIds: string[]; entityNames: string[];\n      caseId: string; severity: 'critical' | 'high' | 'info' | 'warning';\n      location: string; confidenceScore: number; evidenceRef?: string;\n    }\n    ```\n  - `src/data/mockData.ts` requires `mockTimelineEvents` (3 events: `tl-1`, `tl-2`, `tl-3` present in earlier turn transcripts).\n  - `src/pages/TimelinePage.tsx` line 23 has `import { cn } from '../../lib/utils'` which must be `import { cn } from '../lib/utils'`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Workspace Directory**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch`\n- **Virtual Environment**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\.venv` (Python 3.14.7, FastAPI, Uvicorn, SQLAlchemy, NetworkX installed).\n- **Backend Path**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\backend` (PID 18248 listening on `0.0.0.0:8000`).\n- **Frontend Path**: `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Append Missing Types to `scratch/nexus/src/types/index.ts`**:\n   Add `EventCategory` and `TimelineEvent` definitions at the bottom of the file.\n2. **Append Missing Export to `scratch/nexus/src/data/mockData.ts`**:\n   Add `export const mockTimelineEvents: TimelineEvent[] = [...]` (`tl-1`, `tl-2`, `tl-3`).\n3. **Fix Import in `scratch/nexus/src/pages/TimelinePage.tsx`**:\n   Change `import { cn } from '../../lib/utils'` to `import { cn } from '../lib/utils'`.\n4. **Verify TypeScript Build**:\n   Run `npm run build` in `C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus` and ensure it exits with code 0.\n5. **Launch & Verify Both Servers**:\n   - Backend: `& \"..\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`\n   - Frontend: `npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173`\n   - Verify both ports (8000 and 5173) respond with HTTP 200 via `httpx`.\n6. **Report Live URLs to User**:\n   Provide `http://localhost:5173` (Frontend) and `http://localhost:8000/docs` (Backend).\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep existing frontend design and UI components intact.\n- Connect existing pages (`CasesPage`, `DashboardPage`, `NetworkAnalysisPage`, `EntityProfilePage`) to `src/lib/api.ts`.\n- Ensure synthetic Indian data and ethical terminology are consistently maintained across all endpoints and UI displays.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 2 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[AR